# Cursor Rules for baifa-api (BaiFa Power Tracking Backend)

Domain Context:
- Platform: Generator tracking & logistics (BaiFa Power).
- Roles: admin (full control), manager (operations), employee (operator), client (customer portal).
- Documentation: Centralized in `../baifa-docs/`. Business rules in `../baifa-docs/business/business_rules_backend.md`.

Operational Rules:
- NO automatic tests. NO automatic Pint. Run only upon manual request.
- Run all commands via Docker Compose: `docker compose exec app ...`.

Clean Code Guidelines:
- Thin controllers: Form Requests for validation, API Resources for JSON responses. Avoid over-engineering.
- Private endpoints: require `auth:sanctum` and roles where applicable. Public: only /login, /register, /health.
- Logging: Categorized in Spanish (`[CLIENTES_INFO]`, `[CLIENTES_ERROR]`) for Docker monitoring.
- Documentation: Always document in Spanish in `docs/openapi.yaml` and record client rules in `../baifa-docs/business/business_rules_backend.md`.